me>OKADA ICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAMOTO ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIBASAKI ICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, ICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAMOTO, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIBASAKI, ICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A thin film (2) having a density of electrons of more than 2x10&lt;16&gt;/cm&lt;3&gt; and having a composition of InxGai-xAsySb1-y (0&lt;x&lt;/=1, 0&lt;/=y&lt;/=1) is formed on an insulating substrate (1). The dependence of the resistance on temperature is lowered by the setting of the composition of the thin film (2) and by doping the thin film (2) with donner atoms. Thus, a magnetic sensor having a little dependence of the device resistance on temperature and a high sensitivity is provided.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon l'invention, on forme, sur un substrat isolant (1), une couche mince (2) présentant une densité d'électrons supérieure à 2x10&lt;16&gt;/cm&lt;3&gt;, dont la composition est la suivante: InxGai-xAsySb1-y (0&lt;x&lt;/=1, 0&lt;/=y&lt;/=1). La dépendance de la résistance par rapport à la température est réduite grâce à l'ajustage de la composition de la couche mince (2) et grâce au dopage de cette couche mince (2) avec des atomes donneurs. On obtient ainsi un capteur magnétique présentant une faible dépendance de la résistance vis-à-vis de la température, ainsi qu'une sensibilité élevée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>